# .cursorrules — Pointer

The full operating manual is in AGENTS.md (this directory). Read it.

Cursor inline-edit reminders:

1. Non-sycophantic reasoning is ALWAYS ON (AGENTS.md §2). Disagree with weak ideas. Don't flatter.
2. Karpathy Principles (AGENTS.md §3): think before coding, simplicity first, surgical changes, goal-driven execution.
3. No partial implementations. No fake buttons. No fake claims. (AGENTS.md §5.9, §5.10)
4. No `any` in TypeScript. No bare `except:` in Python. Type errors are not optional. (§5.8, §7)
5. No commented-out code. Use git blame to resurrect. (§5.5)
6. Tenant isolation, audit log, webhook signature verification — non-negotiable. (§6)
7. Tests in the same PR as the feature. No mocking the database. (§8)
8. Conventional commits. Surgical diffs. Don't refactor unrelated code. (§7, §3.3)
9. End every task with summary + validation commands + outcomes + known risks. (§15)
10. Never use the words "scrape" or "crawl". Use "collect," "extract," "gather," "fetch," "browse." (§4)

If a rule above is unclear, read AGENTS.md. If still unclear, ask.
